Hi,

I have just started playing nethack and I became a right 
nethack-junkie.  I've _dreamed_ twice already about amulets,
monsters, arqueologists and people wanting to kill me.

I had never played anything like it before, nor any other AD&D  game,
not even any text adventure game, save for a few hours of Zork
a long, long time ago.

Needless to say, I'm being slaughtered mercilessly :).  My highest
score so far was some 69000 when I was very very lucky and found a
cloak of displacement and an amulet of reflection on the second or third
level.  From then on it was a piece of cake until I got  too cheeky and
a guard put me in my own place. You die ...

When I see people with scores of 10^6++ I want to die, literally.

Now, I having problems because I don't know what most of the weapon
are, so I don't use them.  It would be very  helpful if someone posted
a list of them.  I mean the normal ones, not the named/magical/super-power
stuff.  I think these come up naturally during the game and I having good
fun finding out about them myeself. I mean things like:

wakizashi (Is this the short sword, that goes along with the katana ?)
ninja-to
bec-de-corbin
morning-star (A nice warning came up in a fortune cookie about this one,
	      but I don't even know if you are supposed to shoot, wield,
	      or whatever.)

and countless others.  I think many new players would benefit as well.

By the way, I play under X11/linux, and it is really really nice. 
Maybe people who are having problems under DOS should consider switching :)
My only minor gripe is that the high scores list comes up not in a pop-up
window but in the terminal where you started nethack.  If you start it
from a menu in a window manager, it ends up in the shell that started the
X session and you don't see it.  As I die a _lot_, this is important to me :)
I understand it is less critical for more experienced players.

Congrats to the dev team on a job well done.  I'm spending time I don't
have on it.

Bye, and thanks,

